  "statuteText": "652:16-d Accessible Voting System. –\n\n\"Accessible voting system\" shall mean the system chosen by the state in federal elections or by municipalities in local elections to meet the accessibility for individuals with disabilities requirements of section 301 of the Help America Vote Act of 2002, 42 U.S.C. section 15481, 52 U.S.C. section 21081, and Title II of the Americans with Disabilities Act, 42 U.S.C. section 12132, that has the capacity to print a paper ballot marked with the votes chosen by the voter."
